From 66b855ff85c99bc92261c1d4a239f31a8862bcc9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Uzair Aftab <git@uzaaft.me>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 22:16:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] kk: implement VK_EXT_transform_feedback

XFB rides the poly geometry-shader emulation:

- kk_device gains 32KiB of sink pages (RO half reads as zero, RW half is
  a write-discard target); kk_nir_lower_poly lowers
  load_ro_sink_address_poly / ro_to_rw_poly / load_stat_query_address_poly
  / load_provoking_last against them (KK has no VK_EXT_provoking_vertex,
  so the convention is always "first").
- Pipelines whose last pre-raster stage has xfb_info but no app GS get a
  synthesized poly passthrough GS at compile time (KK pipelines are
  monolithic and dynamic topology is class-restricted, so the decomposed
  input primitive is static). Its poly info is mirrored into the VS
  (info.vs.gs) since no GEOMETRY shader object is bound;
  kk_active_gs_info() serves both cases. Output types are float32, not
  AGX's uint32 trick: Metal requires float [[position]] and stage-linked
  varying types.
- kk_launch_gs dispatches the count shader, libkk_prefix_sum_geom and the
  pre-GS program when XFB or TF queries are active; kk_upload_geometry_params
  fills the XFB buffer/offset/counter fields (disabled slots point at the
  device sinks).
- CmdBindTransformFeedbackBuffersEXT / CmdBegin/EndTransformFeedbackEXT
  (counter save/restore via a new libkk_copy_xfb_counters kernel) /
  CmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT (byte counter converted to a regular
  indirect draw by libkk_xfb_indirect_from_counter).
- TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM queries: 2 reports (written, needed) bumped
  directly by the prepasses; Begin/EndQueryIndexedEXT added.

Known gaps: XFB with tessellation pipelines is blocked by the existing
tess+GS gap; pipeline-statistics queries remain unsupported (their
counters land in the sink page).

Verified on Apple M3 Max: passthrough capture of exact vertex data,
app-GS capture, counter buffer = 48 after 3 vertices,
TRANSFORM_FEEDBACK_STREAM query (written=1, needed=1),
vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT re-draw fullscreen-green readback; GS
render test, robustness2, host-pointer import and bobrvm venus-smoke
regressions unchanged.
